BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Daily Guided & Self-Guided Tour of Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20260915T090000
DTEND:20260915T153000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170850Z
UID:737b4502cc0f48952a32b38453cc06@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside the breathtaking home of one of the most prolific 
 inventors of the 20th century\, John Hays Hammond\, Jr. Hammond Castle Mus
 eum is a dynamic STEAM museum\,*blending its historical significance as bo
 th **a historic house museum and a lapidarium. Inside\, you’ll not only 
 discover ancient\, medieval\, and Renaissance architectural elements and a
 rtifacts—including stone archways\, sarcophagi\, grave markers\, and an 
 extraordinary collection of stone and marble works—but you’ll also fin
 d a vibrant museum offering fresh educational and cultural arts programmin
 g. Visitors can explore items from the archival collection that have not b
 een publicly seen in generations\, along with newly curated content and th
 e most up-to-date information on the provenance of many pieces in our coll
 ection. New this season\, the Museum features four temporary exhibits that
  explore John Hays Hammond Jr. as both an individual and a scientific inno
 vator. In the Natalie Hays Hammond Temporary Exhibit Room\, Curatorial Dir
 ector John Leysath presents Spinning Platters with Hammond: Inside the Wor
 ld of Vinyl Records\, on display from April 29th through August 31st. Begi
 nning September 10th and running through the end of the 2025 season on Jan
 uary 4th\, Leysath will showcase” Hammond in Italy: The Love Affair Betw
 een the Hammonds & Italian Culture.”Additionally\, the Inventions Exhibi
 t Room will highlight Hammond’s groundbreaking Videotape Technology duri
 ng the spring and summer months\, followed by Hammond’s ahead-of-their-t
 ime Advertising Signs in the fall and early winter. Listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places\, and a repeated Reader’s Choice Best of No
 rth Shore winner by Northshore Magazine and a Trip Advisor Traveler’s Ch
 oice award recipient for the last three consecutive years\,** you can trus
 t that your visit will be an unforgettable experience. New This Season: Ne
 w Daily Hours and Flexible Arrival Times for Self-Guided Tours Open daily 
 from 9:00 am to 3:30 pm\, with the last entrance at 2:45 pm. The Museum\, 
 Museum Shop\, and grounds close at 3:30 pm. Experience Hammond Castle Muse
 um at your own pace with our new flexible arrival times for self-guided to
 urs. Your ticket grants you entry anytime within designated periods\, ensu
 ring you can arrive stress-free and enjoy your visit to the fullest. Morni
 ng Session: 9:00 am – 11:45 am / Afternoon Session: 11:45 am – 2:30 pm
  Self-guided tours allow you to explore at your own pace. We recommend pla
 nning for at least 60 minutes to experience the Museum’s fascinating gal
 leries\, grounds\, and temporary exhibits. **Accessibility Note: Please be
  aware that at nearly a century old\, the Hammond Castle Museum is not han
 dicapped accessible due to many difficult and winding stairs on the campus
  and within the Museum\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://no
 rthofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammond-castle-muse
 um/2026-09-15/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/daily-guided-self-guided-tour-of-hammo
 nd-castle-museum/2026-09-15/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20260915T130000
DTEND:20260915T160000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170850Z
UID:d51ca06be0306fd0a8f2f2f88d7adf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-09-15/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-0
 9-15/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Land & Sea Club
DTSTART:20260915T150000
DTEND:20260915T170000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170850Z
UID:1bf2ae1a5f9d3033aee4d4a03903ac@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:SESSION 1 RIVER & MARSH ECOLOGY Land & Sea Club brings kids in
 to the working life of the Museum Shipyard to explore\, make\, and learn b
 y doing. For this six-week fall session\, we’ll head outside to investig
 ate the Essex River and salt marsh. Students will explore tides and water 
 quality\, identify plants and animals\, track invasive green crabs\, learn
  about the changing marsh ecosystem\, and develop practical skills for saf
 ely working around boats and the waterfront. This isn’t a classroom prog
 ram moved outside. We’ll use the Shipyard\, river\, marsh\, boats\, and 
 the world around us as the classroom. Ages 10-16 Tuesdays & Thursdays | 3
 –5 PM Six weeks | $75/week Maximum 15 participants No previous experienc
 e is necessary. Come dressed to be outside\, get dirty\, and participate. 
 Come be part of the crew. Love Land & Sea Club? Keep an eye out for future
  sessions. Additional programs may be offered throughout the school year b
 ased on interest.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northof
 boston.org/event/land-sea-club/2026-09-15/
LOCATION:Essex Shipbuilding Museum\, 66 MAIN ST\, ESSEX\, MA\, 01929
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/land-sea-club/2026-09-15/
END:VEVENT
