BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Scholars: Seasonal Rhythms
DTSTART:20261022T090000
DTEND:20261022T120000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170850Z
UID:386ccfb7a4eee788415e7c199cd11c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us in October for weekly homeschool programs exploring th
 e seasonal rhythms of the trails\, woodlands\, farm fields\, and coastline
 s of the Crane Estate and Appleton Farms! October is a great time to see h
 ow nature is changing and getting ready for winter. Participants will expl
 ore the coastline\, trails\, and woodlands of The Crane Estate & Appleton 
 Farms\, while making observations\, taking measurements\, and learning how
  scientists study nature as the seasons change. This is a drop-off program
  that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group work specialized a
 ctivities based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups
 . The class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors a
 s possible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lun
 ch and water bottle. Homeschool Scholars: Seasonal Rhythms- This 4-class s
 eries program takes place on Thursdays from 9am-12pm on October 1\, 8\, 15
 \, & 22. Crane Estate: October 1 & 15 Appleton Farms: October 8 & 22 Tuiti
 on for the 4 classes is $275 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers.
  Registration covers all listed session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston
 \nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-scholars-seasonal
 -rhythms/2026-10-22/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-scholars-seasonal-rhythms/2
 026-10-22/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Land & Sea Club
DTSTART:20261022T150000
DTEND:20261022T170000
DTSTAMP:20260914T170850Z
UID:2517ccd45d8877dc45b95d462b5d4f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:SESSION 1 RIVER & MARSH ECOLOGY Land & Sea Club brings kids in
 to the working life of the Museum Shipyard to explore\, make\, and learn b
 y doing. For this six-week fall session\, we’ll head outside to investig
 ate the Essex River and salt marsh. Students will explore tides and water 
 quality\, identify plants and animals\, track invasive green crabs\, learn
  about the changing marsh ecosystem\, and develop practical skills for saf
 ely working around boats and the waterfront. This isn’t a classroom prog
 ram moved outside. We’ll use the Shipyard\, river\, marsh\, boats\, and 
 the world around us as the classroom. Ages 10-16 Tuesdays & Thursdays | 3
 –5 PM Six weeks | $75/week Maximum 15 participants No previous experienc
 e is necessary. Come dressed to be outside\, get dirty\, and participate. 
 Come be part of the crew. Love Land & Sea Club? Keep an eye out for future
  sessions. Additional programs may be offered throughout the school year b
 ased on interest.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northof
 boston.org/event/land-sea-club/2026-10-22/
LOCATION:Essex Shipbuilding Museum\, 66 MAIN ST\, ESSEX\, MA\, 01929
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/land-sea-club/2026-10-22/
END:VEVENT
